cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use twas-xcal, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "twas-xcal: ancestry-aware null calibration for transcriptome-wide association studies"
abstract: >-
  XCAL-t is an ancestry-aware null calibration for summary-statistic TWAS tests
  under polygenic backgrounds: an ancestry-matched LD panel, a bias-corrected
  estimator of the polygenic variance term, GWAS allele-frequency SD scaling,
  and a jackknife Satterthwaite t reference for LD-panel noise and uncertainty
  in the LD-score-regression intercept and slope. Includes a benchmark that counts false positives
  against an exactly known simulated null (infinitesimal and sparse architectures)
  a real-genotype benchmark (1000 Genomes x MESA) and a Biobank Japan height
  application.
